<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indragiri Hilir Regency</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Indragiri Hilir is a regency on the east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riau">Riau</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, covering the lower course and delta of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indragiri-river">Indragiri River</a>. Its capital is Tembilahan. The regency was formed from lands of the former Indragiri Sultanate, and its economy rests on coconut plantations, fishing and river trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indragiri-hilir-regency.jpg" alt="Indragiri Hilir Regency" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ewesewes at Indonesian Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lokasi_Riau_Kabupaten_Indragiri_Hilir.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
